<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1motivation">
<title>Motivation</title><para><linebreak/>
 A selection of inline functions for float comparisons that account for numerical precision. Function names should be self-explanatory. Functions can be traced back to Knuth&apos;s book and were found on: <ulink url="http://stackoverflow.com/questions/17333/most-effective-way-for-float-and-double-comparison">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/17333/most-effective-way-for-float-and-double-comparison</ulink></para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="compare_floats_8h_1testing">
<title>Testing</title><para><linebreak/>
 code was taken as is without further testing </para>
</sect1>
